WEBVTT

00:02.120 --> 00:05.665
"It seems today that all you see

00:05.790 --> 00:09.126
"Is violence in movies and sex on TV

00:09.211 --> 00:12.964
"But where are those
good old-fashioned values

00:13.090 --> 00:15.049
"On which we used to rely?

00:15.800 --> 00:19.136
"Lucky there's a family guy

00:19.220 --> 00:24.225
"Lucky there's a man who positively
can do all the things that make us

00:24.350 --> 00:25.684
"Laugh and cry

00:25.809 --> 00:31.232
"He's a family guy

00:34.151 --> 00:37.363
Some of this stuff... you wonder
who would need it in bulk.

00:37.488 --> 00:40.075
I mean, like watermelons.

00:41.658 --> 00:44.037
Touchй, CostMart.

00:44.162 --> 00:46.329
- Brian, will you watch Stewie?
- Sure.

00:46.454 --> 00:49.876
Please keep a close eye on him.
Remember what happened last time.

00:51.335 --> 00:55.838
- Stewie, get down before you hurt yourself.
- Shut up! You're not my mother!

00:55.922 --> 00:58.634
- Good God! Are you all right?
- Fine. Why do you ask?

01:00.636 --> 01:06.767
Mmm, delicious. I will seriously
consider purchasing this product.

01:07.935 --> 01:10.938
Oh, what have we here? May I partake?

01:11.063 --> 01:13.148
Mmm.

01:15.025 --> 01:19.070
Sausage-san.
Plan to buy for samurai buddies.

01:19.195 --> 01:23.450
You don't have to keep moving to the back.
You can have as many as you want.

01:23.575 --> 01:25.119
What are you talking about?

01:25.244 --> 01:27.330
- Can I have more sausage?
- Yeah, me too?

01:28.246 --> 01:32.834
They got a great deal on pianos if you buy
a four-pack. Meg, help me get these down.

01:32.959 --> 01:35.044
- Lois?
- Oh, my gosh.

01:35.128 --> 01:37.214
I don't believe this.

01:37.339 --> 01:42.135
Ross Fishman, is that really you? I haven't
seen you since college. How are you?

01:42.218 --> 01:45.264
Great. Wow, Lois! You haven't aged a bit.

01:45.347 --> 01:48.391
Oh. Thank you.

01:48.391 --> 01:52.978
This 12-pack of fungicide
is for my daughter Meg.

01:53.062 --> 01:55.690
Help me.

01:58.401 --> 02:00.903
- He's funny.
- Is it 1981?

02:02.029 --> 02:03.823
Ah, yes, there you are!

02:03.907 --> 02:09.037
You people at the Industrial Adhesives
Corporation know how to make a tasty glue.

02:09.121 --> 02:11.122
Well, then, let the banquet begin.

02:11.206 --> 02:15.376
- What are you doing? Don't eat that.
- For God's sake, don't be such a nerd.

02:15.501 --> 02:18.630
I'm keeping an eye on you.
If Lois sees this, she'll kill me.

02:18.713 --> 02:22.883
- You can let go of my hand now.
- You can let go of mine.

02:35.103 --> 02:36.855
- Oh...
- Crap.

02:36.980 --> 02:40.109
I can't tell you how wonderful
it's been to see you.

02:40.109 --> 02:43.237
It's a crime that it's been so long.
We were so close.

02:43.320 --> 02:45.823
We could get together for coffee, catch up.

02:45.949 --> 02:49.493
Well... I don't know, Ross. I'm married now.

02:49.576 --> 02:53.956
So am I. Does that mean we're not allowed
to stay in touch with old friends?

02:54.081 --> 02:57.625
Tell you what. If you change
your mind, here's my card.

02:59.086 --> 03:02.005
Look, Dad. They have 12-packs of kidneys!

03:02.088 --> 03:04.925
You got to buy the cooler, too.
That's how they get you.

03:07.094 --> 03:09.388
- OK, thanks.
- Well?

03:09.513 --> 03:12.933
The good news is they make
a solvent that'll get us unstuck.

03:13.058 --> 03:15.226
But it takes two weeks for delivery.

03:15.351 --> 03:18.480
We're stuck like this for a bloody fortnight?!

03:18.564 --> 03:21.400
- You cannot tell Lois about this.
- What if I do?

03:21.400 --> 03:26.404
- I have pictures of you in her wedding dress.
- You said there was no film in that camera!

03:26.488 --> 03:30.784
- Stewie, it's time to change your diaper.
- Mind if I watch?

03:32.118 --> 03:35.997
And I'm ashamed of myself
that I let Peter's jealousy prevent me

03:36.081 --> 03:39.542
from rekindling an old friendship
just because it was with a man.

03:39.625 --> 03:43.379
Peter's not very understanding
when it comes to you and other men.

03:43.504 --> 03:45.798
Like that time at the movies?

03:48.175 --> 03:51.929
I... I... this is... My, this is terribly awkward.

03:52.055 --> 03:54.849
But I... I wanted to tell you something.

03:54.974 --> 03:58.603
But I... I seem to be
so charmingly befuddled.

03:58.728 --> 04:02.773
- Ah, that Hugh Grant is so handsome.
- Oh, is that how it is?

04:02.898 --> 04:05.609
Come here, you home-wrecking bastard!

04:05.692 --> 04:08.947
Don't do it, Dad! He's bigger than you!

04:09.030 --> 04:11.240
And when you went to that concert?

04:11.323 --> 04:15.827
Thank you. Thank you very much.
This next one is for all the ladies out there.

04:19.789 --> 04:21.959
Then there was last Saturday night.

04:22.085 --> 04:27.173
- Oh, look at that handsome man.
- You son of a bitch!

04:27.298 --> 04:30.299
I can't let Peter's irrational
emotions run my life!

04:30.425 --> 04:33.761
I'm gonna call Ross and see
if it's not too late for his offer.

04:33.845 --> 04:35.931
- Would you mind finishing up?
- Sure.

04:36.057 --> 04:38.975
Yes, do you like cleaning my doody, Brian?

04:38.975 --> 04:44.482
Say it. Say "I like cleaning your doody,
Stewie. " Ha! Don't forget the taint.

04:49.903 --> 04:53.573
TC, fly the chopper around the island.
I'll talk to the women.

04:53.656 --> 04:57.536
- Tattoo here will look out for the kidnappers.
- Higgins.

04:57.536 --> 05:00.747
We'll need security to unlock
the gate for me. OK, Tattoo?

05:00.872 --> 05:02.957
- It's Higgins.
- What?

05:02.957 --> 05:05.043
The name is Higgins.

05:06.794 --> 05:09.297
- What's your name?
- Tattoo.

05:10.048 --> 05:15.345
Oh, Peter. I'm just...
gonna go out for a few hours.

05:15.470 --> 05:18.473
So, I... I'll return in... a few hours.

05:18.598 --> 05:21.100
Yeah, I'll do it when this is over.

05:21.184 --> 05:23.896
Hey, Lois, can you grab me a beer?

05:24.021 --> 05:25.980
- Lois?
- Dad, I think she went out.

05:26.105 --> 05:28.066
- Then you be Lois.
- OK.

05:28.191 --> 05:32.028
Lois, can you grab me a beer?
Oh, my God! You've really let yourself go!

05:32.154 --> 05:35.156
Maybe if you bought me
nice clothes once in a while!

05:36.741 --> 05:40.995
Peter Griffin, we know you're in there!
Come out with your hands up!

05:41.120 --> 05:43.622
Fooled ya!

05:44.247 --> 05:46.334
You sure did. What the hell is this?

05:46.334 --> 05:50.296
The new police surveillance van.
We're going on a beer run. Wanna join us?

05:50.379 --> 05:52.881
I quit drinking. I might be an alcoholic.

05:53.006 --> 05:54.466
- What?
- Oh, my God!

05:54.550 --> 05:59.472
Fooled ya! Come on. Let's go drink
till we can't feel feelings any more.

05:59.555 --> 06:03.642
This van has the latest in
law-enforcement technology. Watch.

06:04.351 --> 06:07.897
Suspect! Suspect!
You have the right to remain silent!

06:08.022 --> 06:09.565
Sweet.

06:09.690 --> 06:11.650
- Let me try.
- Cleveland, don't!

06:11.775 --> 06:16.238
Minority suspect! Minority suspect!
Danger, he's got a gun!

06:16.363 --> 06:19.991
Oh! Ow! Ow! Oh! Ow! Oh! Ow!

06:22.285 --> 06:23.871
Hey, Joe! The van's gone!

06:23.954 --> 06:27.624
It's got a cloaking device that
disguises it as two homeless guys

06:27.624 --> 06:30.126
fighting over a wedge of cheese.

06:32.212 --> 06:35.215
Peter, isn't that Lois
over there in that diner?

06:35.340 --> 06:38.885
- Why would Lois be there? I already ate.
- Take a look.

06:38.968 --> 06:42.222
Oh, my God! That is Lois!
Why the hell would she...

06:42.305 --> 06:43.973
Whoa. I can see your skin cells.

06:44.098 --> 06:47.311
I saw you on Scientific American.
You looked great.

06:47.436 --> 06:51.899
- Please! Where my eyes are half-closed?
- God, just take the damn compliment!

06:55.444 --> 06:59.739
- What is Lois doing with another man?
- Is it possible she's a whore?

06:59.823 --> 07:05.036
Just on weekends? To help pay for
her mom's dialysis? As in my fantasy?

07:05.161 --> 07:07.454
Let's start over. Hi, I'm Quagmire.

07:07.454 --> 07:10.792
- I wish I knew what she was saying.
- I think I can help.

07:10.792 --> 07:16.505
Oh, your wife and children are beautiful. It's
so good to catch up, Ross. I'm glad I called.

07:16.630 --> 07:19.843
I'm glad you did, too.
Was your husband OK with you coming?

07:19.968 --> 07:23.387
Uh... Yes, he turned out
to be just fine with it.

07:25.598 --> 07:29.017
All right. Let's see what we can pick up.

07:29.143 --> 07:33.105
Please don't spit in my eggs.
Please don't spit in my eggs.

07:33.189 --> 07:36.859
Thank you for the eggs!
I hope he didn't spit in my eggs.

07:36.942 --> 07:39.361
Doug, I spit in that guy's eggs.

07:39.445 --> 07:42.698
Our armies are ready.
We will leave the sewers

07:42.781 --> 07:45.409
and strike back at the humans
in the overworld.

07:46.868 --> 07:49.872
I'm glad we both found someone
to make us happy.

07:49.997 --> 07:52.999
I enjoy being with you, Ross.
I'm having a great time.

07:53.124 --> 07:57.587
Oh, my God! That's who that is.
Ross Fishman, Lois's old boyfriend.

07:57.712 --> 08:00.090
- We're losing them.
- I gotta hear more.

08:00.215 --> 08:02.592
The power's not supposed to go that high!

08:02.717 --> 08:05.221
Damn itch. I wonder who gave it to me.

08:05.304 --> 08:10.643
Probably that skank who needed a ride.
Last time I do somebody a favour.

08:10.726 --> 08:13.854
Oh, God! They must have heard me!
Oh, God! I can hear me!

08:23.655 --> 08:27.201
Ugh! What the hell
do you think you're doing?!

08:27.326 --> 08:29.703
I'm cleaning myself.

08:29.826 --> 08:33.664
You were clean 15 minutes ago.
Now you're just on vacation.

08:34.623 --> 08:38.878
So, Lois is seeing old boyfriends, huh?
Well, two can play at that game.

08:39.003 --> 08:41.798
I just gotta find my little black book.

08:57.980 --> 08:59.440
Ah, here it is.

09:04.654 --> 09:09.533
- Brenda?
- Peter! Oh, my God. It's been 25 years!

09:09.658 --> 09:13.079
Yeah. So, I guess you're married now, huh?

09:13.204 --> 09:15.498
Yeah.

09:17.582 --> 09:21.419
Hey, Ricky, you were right! I was pregnant!

09:23.715 --> 09:26.550
Hey, what's up, Pete? Long time no see.

09:26.550 --> 09:28.927
Patty, the years have been great to you.

09:29.053 --> 09:33.099
- I owe that to my better half.
- Who is it, sir?

09:36.142 --> 09:40.522
- Angie?
- Peter? Oh, my God! Oh, my God! Come in!

09:48.946 --> 09:51.158
Uh... what is all this stuff?

09:51.241 --> 09:55.204
Peter, I have been waiting
for this moment for 25 years!

09:55.329 --> 09:57.706
I haven't washed my hand
since you touched it.

09:57.830 --> 09:59.917
Oh, my God! That's disgusting!

10:00.000 --> 10:05.004
And look! Look! I left the toilet just
as it was the night we went to the prom.

10:05.129 --> 10:08.550
It's the little piece of you
that's kept your memory alive.

10:08.675 --> 10:11.261
But now I have you back.

10:11.386 --> 10:14.597
Oh, well. At least I still have you.

10:14.722 --> 10:16.808
You hungry?

10:17.851 --> 10:20.563
Oh, crap.

10:21.479 --> 10:22.938
Let me handle this.

10:23.063 --> 10:28.569
You were going 65, fella. That's ten miles
over the... Why are you holding his hand?

10:28.694 --> 10:30.654
- We met on the Internet.
- Shut up!

10:30.780 --> 10:34.618
He lured me to the park with promises
of candy and funny stories.

10:34.743 --> 10:39.206
- Ever hear of super industrial adhesive?
- Actually, yes, we have.

10:46.629 --> 10:51.509
- Dad, why do you keep looking at the door?
- Oh, Meg. You and your drugs.

10:51.634 --> 10:54.136
I wonder who that could be.

10:55.471 --> 11:00.267
- Peter Gifford?
- My God! Dora, my old girlfriend.

11:00.392 --> 11:04.855
What a surprise that you would look me up!
You always thought I was so handsome.

11:04.980 --> 11:08.107
Peter, can I see you in the other room?

11:08.191 --> 11:09.985
- Yeah, go. Say it.
- Should I?

11:10.069 --> 11:12.779
- I can't.
- Just say it.

11:12.905 --> 11:17.075
How far can you get this banana...
I can't say it. She's looking right at me.

11:17.159 --> 11:19.161
What the hell is this about?

11:19.244 --> 11:23.207
- It's about you and Ross Fishman!
- What?!

11:23.332 --> 11:26.126
I saw you and him breaking
the Fifth Commandment!

11:26.251 --> 11:28.837
Congress passes these things for a reason!

11:28.962 --> 11:33.550
That's it! You're suffocating me
with your jealousy. I can't take it any more.

11:33.633 --> 11:38.221
I'm calling a marriage counsellor.
I can't even have coffee with a friend!

11:38.346 --> 11:42.725
- What is your problem?!
- You want to know what my problem is?

11:42.808 --> 11:45.729
- I love too much!
- What are you talking about?

11:45.854 --> 11:48.857
- Don't you see? We're alive!
- You're scaring me.

11:48.982 --> 11:54.278
Good! Embrace the fear! Dance with me,
Lois. Dance the dance of life!

11:56.155 --> 11:58.365
Maybe you should call that counsellor.

12:00.450 --> 12:03.162
Mr and Mrs Griffin,
I've reviewed your situation.

12:03.245 --> 12:06.082
- I have a suggestion.
- We'll do whatever it takes.

12:06.165 --> 12:09.085
I'd like to put video cameras
in every room of your house

12:09.210 --> 12:11.796
so I can observe your
uncensored behaviour.

12:11.922 --> 12:16.175
Just like that show Big Brother.
Except somebody'll be watching.

12:18.886 --> 12:20.971
I've looked through the footage.

12:21.096 --> 12:26.184
I've compiled an accurate cross section
of your home life. Here are the results.

12:28.813 --> 12:31.398
- Peter, give Chris a spanking.
- OK.

12:31.524 --> 12:34.652
Chris, I'm watching the game.
You know what to do.

12:35.693 --> 12:38.614
Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow!

12:38.697 --> 12:41.951
This hurts me more than it hurts you. Ow!

12:42.159 --> 12:45.162
"Dear Diary, Kevin is so hot. "

12:45.287 --> 12:48.499
"Today he was out
in the yard raking leaves. "

12:48.624 --> 12:52.669
"God, I wish he'd throw me
into that pile of leaves. "

12:54.671 --> 12:58.509
Hey, what's everybody...
Oh, my God! My diary! I hate you all!

13:01.136 --> 13:02.888
Keep going.

13:03.222 --> 13:08.018
No. It's step, hip, step, pivot.
Are you trying to piss off the volcano?

13:08.309 --> 13:10.729
Get my back, would you?

13:10.729 --> 13:13.857
Oh, that's it. Ooh, that feels good.

13:14.065 --> 13:18.444
- Can you give me a hand with this jar?
- Oh, for heaven's sake, Peter.

13:18.444 --> 13:21.365
Gotcha.

13:23.951 --> 13:26.577
To be honest, I've never seen
such dysfunction.

13:26.660 --> 13:30.832
Mr and Mrs Griffin, what I'm about
to suggest may seem unorthodox.

13:30.957 --> 13:35.961
I recommend a trial separation, during which
time I advise that you date other people.

13:36.044 --> 13:38.881
I believe this will help you
gather perspective.

13:38.965 --> 13:41.050
- Date other people?!
- Oh, my God!

13:41.175 --> 13:45.220
I realise this is upsetting.
That's why I've invited Howie Mandel

13:45.345 --> 13:50.017
to lighten the mood by blowing up
a surgical glove with his nose.

14:07.869 --> 14:09.744
This feels really weird, Lois.

14:09.829 --> 14:14.124
I know. But maybe the doctor's right.
This time apart could be good for us.

14:14.124 --> 14:17.961
I don't know. Splitting up didn't work
too well for Pacman and his wife.

14:18.086 --> 14:21.507
- Forget about her.
- You're too good for her anyway.

14:21.632 --> 14:24.551
- Cheer up, man.
- Hey, you want to eat us? Huh?

14:24.634 --> 14:27.553
- We're turning blue!
- I've got nowhere to run.

14:27.679 --> 14:30.265
He's gonna get us!

14:30.391 --> 14:32.058
- Oh.
- Oh.

14:32.058 --> 14:35.063
He's not budging.
Come on. Let's go to Qbert's.

14:35.188 --> 14:40.400
- I appreciate you putting me up, Cleveland.
- Our house is your house, Peter.

14:40.484 --> 14:44.447
I'd sit here and chat, but I need
to get back upstairs to Loretta

14:44.572 --> 14:49.034
because it's our anniversary
and the getting's good.

14:49.160 --> 14:54.789
Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow!

14:54.872 --> 14:59.794
When is it gonna be my turn?
Ow! Ow! Ow! Ow!

15:01.129 --> 15:03.757
You are welcome to stay
as long as you like.

15:03.839 --> 15:07.302
Thanks, Muriel. So, what do you guys
do for fun around here?

15:07.385 --> 15:11.055
We like to watch old movies
while listening to "Hotel California"

15:11.055 --> 15:13.642
to see if it syncs up in a significant way.

15:13.766 --> 15:16.143
And so far, no. Nothing has.

15:19.480 --> 15:21.357
- Hello?
- Is Peter there?

15:21.482 --> 15:24.193
Oh, hi, Quagmire. No, Peter's not home.

15:24.276 --> 15:28.363
We're... we're having
some minor marital problems.

15:28.448 --> 15:32.535
Our therapist has advised us
to date other people.

15:32.535 --> 15:35.956
- Hey, Lois, you want to go out?
- What? I don't know, Glen.

15:36.081 --> 15:39.625
Peter and I just separated.
I feel like I need more time.

15:41.710 --> 15:44.631
- How about now?
- We are supposed to see other people.

15:44.714 --> 15:47.967
I guess it's better to go out
with you than some sex pervert.

15:48.050 --> 15:50.469
I'm in! Giggetty-gaggety-gaggety-goo!

15:55.891 --> 15:59.436
Oh. God blast it!
Will you hold it for five seconds?!

16:03.691 --> 16:05.275
OK.

16:07.236 --> 16:11.115
So, Mr Griffin, how does it feel
to be a bachelor on the prowl again?

16:11.198 --> 16:15.786
It's not as great as you'd think. I don't have
the same way with women that I used to.

16:17.246 --> 16:20.082
That was nice. That was nice.

16:20.165 --> 16:24.670
I had a great time with you today,
beautiful stranger. What's your sign?

16:26.630 --> 16:29.549
Gross. I still think
you're neat, though.

16:29.674 --> 16:33.511
You should try a video dating service.
That's how Muriel and I met.

16:33.636 --> 16:36.848
Let me show you Mort's tape.
He was so charming.

16:38.308 --> 16:42.604
Agh! Oh, my eyes! Could you please
turn down that very bright light?

16:42.687 --> 16:45.524
It's burning my retinas.

16:45.608 --> 16:47.817
Ladies, I'm a very desperate man.

16:47.900 --> 16:52.196
My name is Mort and I live with my mother.
And I have very low standards.

16:52.279 --> 16:55.950
Oh, God!
There's blood in my mucus!

16:59.912 --> 17:02.915
Agh! What the hell is wrong with you?!

17:04.084 --> 17:06.795
Hey, there's the mail! Oh, finally.

17:09.922 --> 17:12.634
It takes an hour for the solvent to take effect.

17:12.717 --> 17:17.847
What takes an hour? We could watch
Rita Rudner do five minutes of stand-up.

17:17.847 --> 17:18.973
Ba-zing.

17:19.098 --> 17:21.810
We're gonna have a swell time tonight, Lois.

17:21.893 --> 17:25.354
Thank you for being such a good friend
and looking after me.

17:25.354 --> 17:28.483
No problem. It's chilly out,
so I brought you a jacket.

17:28.566 --> 17:32.444
- Oh. No, thanks. I'll be fine.
- Please?

17:36.073 --> 17:41.704
Muriel and I feel that you need to follow
your therapist's advice and start dating.

17:41.829 --> 17:45.249
- Jeez, Mort. I don't know if I'm ready.
- Come on, stud.

17:45.374 --> 17:47.960
We've set it up for you
to go out with our niece.

17:48.085 --> 17:50.796
Honey! Come on out here
and meet Peter Griffin.

17:51.504 --> 17:54.340
This is our niece, Jennifer Love Hewitt.

17:54.340 --> 17:57.260
- Nice to meet you.
- All right, I'm getting up.

17:57.344 --> 18:02.140
Hi. Peter Griffin. We can go anywhere except
the disco. They don't let me in any more.

18:10.398 --> 18:14.444
Ow! Crafty Mexicans and your glass candy.

18:17.697 --> 18:20.491
- What's going on?
- There's a girl in that well.

18:20.616 --> 18:23.953
- Oh, my God!
- Nobody has arms long enough to reach her.

18:23.953 --> 18:27.499
Except that guy. But he's helping
that woman tickle a midget.

18:27.583 --> 18:32.711
Tee-hee. Stop it. Tee-hee.

18:33.964 --> 18:36.341
Oh, God, you want to rescue her, don't you?

18:36.466 --> 18:40.845
It's times like this I wish they'd
used me for stem-cell research.

18:40.845 --> 18:42.388
Help me!

18:42.513 --> 18:47.393
It rubs the lotion on its skin,
or else it gets the hose again. Ha!

18:47.518 --> 18:50.438
All right, I'm gonna lower you in.

18:51.271 --> 18:55.109
I just noticed. How often do you see
a 17th-century well in this day and age?

18:55.234 --> 18:59.197
- Hurry up. The glue's wearing off!
- All right, all right!

19:06.078 --> 19:08.456
We're not stuck together any more.

19:08.581 --> 19:10.958
- Thank God!
- You said it.

19:11.083 --> 19:13.670
- Want to hold hands on the walk home?
- Sure.

19:13.795 --> 19:16.296
Susie! Thank God you're all right!

19:16.380 --> 19:19.007
Wait a minute. This isn't my little girl.

19:19.091 --> 19:21.594
Hey, that was my wife!

19:21.719 --> 19:22.762
- Tee-hee!
- Tee-hee!

19:24.846 --> 19:27.350
- I Know What You Did Last Summer?
- Never heard of it.

19:27.433 --> 19:29.434
- The Devil and Daniel Webster?
- Nope.

19:29.517 --> 19:32.354
- Party of Five?
- Was that a porno?

19:32.354 --> 19:36.316
Sometimes you gotta do a lot of crap
before they put you in anything decent.

19:36.400 --> 19:41.113
The food here is fantastic.
This is where I took Lois on our first date.

19:41.197 --> 19:43.614
You ordered a pie for an appetiser?

19:43.698 --> 19:48.077
I'll go to the john and fire one out in five
minutes. That should make room for dinner.

19:48.203 --> 19:51.623
- Here's your table, Mr Quagmire.
- Thanks. How about drinks?

19:51.748 --> 19:55.168
Martini for you and the usual
roofie colada for your date?

19:55.294 --> 19:58.838
No, no, no. I wouldn't bring...
A glass of wine.

19:59.881 --> 20:03.509
Oh, my God! That's Jennifer Love Hewitt!

20:03.634 --> 20:07.806
Wow! I wonder who she's here with.
She could date any man she wanted to.

20:09.765 --> 20:11.851
There. Made lots of room.

20:11.976 --> 20:16.230
That sign in the bathroom about washing
your hands, that's for the staff, right?

20:16.355 --> 20:19.483
- Technically, yes.
- That's what I thought. Great.

20:19.567 --> 20:22.612
Oh, man! These all look good,
every one of 'em.

20:22.695 --> 20:24.364
- You want some bread?
- No!

20:24.489 --> 20:26.865
Peter, is that you?

20:26.990 --> 20:29.285
Peter?! Oh, no! I can't let him see me!

20:29.285 --> 20:33.247
It's OK, Quagmire. We're just doing
what the therapist said to do.

20:33.330 --> 20:36.793
Peter, I think it's great you're out
with Jennifer Love Hewitt.

20:36.876 --> 20:39.295
Hi. I loved you in Heartbreakers.

20:39.378 --> 20:41.673
You be on your best behaviour.

20:42.214 --> 20:45.343
- Here you go, sweetheart. Open up.
- No!

20:45.343 --> 20:48.261
There you go. Isn't this romantic?

20:48.345 --> 20:53.267
That's it! You have got to be the most vile,
disgusting human being I've ever met!

20:53.267 --> 20:57.645
And I have never been
more turned-on in my life.

20:58.982 --> 21:01.817
Hold on, toots!
I don't care what our therapist says.

21:01.900 --> 21:06.070
I won't stand by and watch my husband
lock lips with another woman! Beat it!

21:06.195 --> 21:08.491
- What's your problem, grandma?
- You are!

21:08.574 --> 21:11.076
And I only saw Heartbreakers on a plane!

21:11.202 --> 21:14.329
And the flight was delayed,
so the headphones were free!

21:14.413 --> 21:16.498
Wow. That was pretty cool, Lois.

21:16.623 --> 21:18.709
I guess I finally understand...

21:23.171 --> 21:25.382
You better run, you little bitch!

21:25.382 --> 21:29.136
I guess I finally understand
how you can get so jealous sometimes.

21:29.219 --> 21:32.472
Seeing her kiss you like that
just made me crazy.

21:32.472 --> 21:36.851
I guess we're gonna have to learn
to control our jealousy... together.

21:36.935 --> 21:38.102
Together.

21:38.185 --> 21:40.063
Ma'am, you dropped your napkin.

21:40.188 --> 21:41.647
Here's your drink, sir.

21:41.731 --> 21:44.776
We'll work on it later. I love you, Lois.

21:44.776 --> 21:46.654
I love you too, Peter.

21:49.155 --> 21:52.575
What a couple of freaks.
God, I need a drink.

21:52.700 --> 21:55.204
Waiter! Martini and a roofie colada.

21:55.205 --> 22:56.205
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru